  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#34950 (Window Masking) and PowerToys#48566 (Restrict App Sharing) both ask for the same thing. They want chosen apps or windows hidden from screen sharing, recording and screenshots, using WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE, with name matching and hotkeys. PowerToys doesn't offer this today, and neither ticket gives a fix or workaround. #48566 was closed as a duplicate of #46333, which I couldn't open, so I can't confirm what it says. Please subscribe to #46333 for updates and add your Outlook and Teams use case there. Until then, check your screen before you share. You can also share a single window instead of the whole screen. Third-party tools such as Invisiwind and winhider are mentioned in #34950. They hide windows from capture, but they don't detect newly opened windows."
 },
